{
	"_doc": "Boarding (docs/BOARDING.md, scripts/board/). The sites the soldier explores on foot: a derelict, an abandoned station, a pirate nest, or the wreck of a ship you beat. All numbers are here. kinds: per site kind (the `board` effect's kind): bands (the layouts, one picked per site: R is a band of rooms, C a corridor between them), interior (the widest band, in cells), room_h and room_w (a room's inside size, [min, max]), hull (the enemy-table faction whose hull ops shape the outline; '' = the region's faction, else clans), weights of the room purposes (airlock is always one room, picked from the rooms at either end of a band), min/max (rooms of a purpose a site has at least/most), hack and card (how many doors are locked, [min, max]: a hack door opens after holding E for `hack_s`; a card door wants the keycard that lies in a container of a room the airlock reaches without it), loop (the chance a pair of side-by-side rooms get a door between them), emergency (the chance a room has a red emergency light), prop_mult (x the props of every room), loot_mult (x the counts of every roll), locked_bonus (x the props of a room behind a locked door), blueprints (the chance of 0, 1, 2 blueprints in the site), logs ([min, max] derelict logs on offer), bonus (outcomes added to every container table of the kind), names (pool for the site's name). props: the site-only layer. size [w, h] (a pallet lies along a wall: it turns), blocks (the soldier cannot walk through), loot (a container: it has contents), rolls ([min, max] rolls of its table), hold (seconds of holding E to open it), table (a table that is not the room's purpose's), bp (weight of holding a blueprint), log (weight of holding a log). rooms: per purpose, the props it gets as [{prop, n: [min, max]}] and the tint it is drawn with; bp is the weight of the room for a blueprint. tables: weighted outcomes as in data/debris.json `roll` ({weight, item, count: [min, max]}); item is a material, an item or a part (cargo), credits or fuel. blueprint: weights of the recipe levels (fab_level 1-3) by the campaign's tier. A blueprint slot becomes a recipe the ship does not know when the container is opened, else `fallback`.",
